&lt;p&gt;SMX is seeking an experienced Data Strategist &amp;amp; Analytics Specialist to serve as the primary data authority for our organization&#39;s Theater/Tactical Mission Network (TMN) operations. This individual will be responsible for the full data lifecycle — from sourcing and validation through workflow design and strategic planning — ensuring that data assets are accurate, actionable, and efficiently utilized across all supported units and subcontractor deliverables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position requires an active DoD Secret clearance with Top Secret SCI eligibility which requires US citizenship for work on DoD contracts.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties &amp;amp; Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data Source Validation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, vet, and validate data sources for accuracy, reliability, completeness, and relevance to mission requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct structured assessments of data providers to determine operational and analytical value, and provide go/no-go recommendations to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a registry of approved, conditional, and rejected data sources with supporting rationale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data Visualization Review (DVR) Oversight&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and quality-assure Data Visualization Review (DVR) products created by subcontractors in response to supported unit Requests for Information (RFIs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess DVR deliverables against defined standards for accuracy, design fidelity, analytical integrity, and alignment with the originating RFI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide written feedback, approval, or rejection of subcontractor products, and coordinate revisions as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TMN Data Strategy Development&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, document, and maintain a comprehensive TMN Data Strategy that aligns data collection, management, and dissemination practices with organizational and mission objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify capability gaps in current data infrastructure and recommend improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish data governance frameworks including ownership, stewardship, quality standards, and lifecycle policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data Usage &amp;amp; Utilization Efficiency&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze current data usage patterns and identify redundancies, inefficiencies, and underutilized assets across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement best practices to maximize the value extracted from existing data resources while reducing waste and duplication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with supported units and internal stakeholders to align data consumption with operational priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data Workflow Design &amp;amp; Implementation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, document, and optimize end-to-end data workflows, including ingestion, processing, storage, access, and dissemination pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize workflow procedures to ensure repeatability, traceability, and quality control across all data operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with technical teams to automate or streamline manual data processes where feasible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data Provider Evaluation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct structured evaluations of current and prospective data providers to assess the value, reliability, and mission relevance of their offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and apply a repeatable provider assessment methodology, including criteria such as data freshness, coverage, accuracy, licensing, and cost-benefit analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce provider validation reports and present findings and recommendations to decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills/Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Data Science, Information Systems, Operations Research, Computer Science, or a related field (Master&#39;s preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in data analysis, data management, or a related discipline, preferably in a defense, intelligence, or government contracting environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience reviewing and evaluating data products or visualizations for technical accuracy and analytical quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data governance, data quality frameworks, and lifecycle management principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing or contributing to organizational data strategies or roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with data visualization tools (e.g., Tableau, Power BI, ArcGIS, or similar platforms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with structured data environments, relational databases, and common data formats (JSON, XML, CSV, shapefiles, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills; ability to produce clear technical documentation and present findings to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have an active DoD Secret security clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills/Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within or in direct support of military or DoD organizational structures, particularly in a TMN, C2, or ISR context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with RFI/DVR processes and subcontractor product review workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of geospatial data sources and GEOINT products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data pipeline tools (e.g., Apache NiFi, Databricks, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications such as Certified Data Management Professional (CDMP), CompTIA Data+, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DoD Top Secret and TS-SCI preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
